 looking for extra clinical  input  so they lend a real clinical eye to the  information that we're providing  okay thank you  we've um had a couple questions about  input files  so  what kind of variants can qci interpret  one process and interpret  and what file types can be  inputted into the informatic system  yeah i'm happy to comment on that um  so um casa interpret one is the um  tertiary analysis solution um so  if it goes straight into pc interface  one this standard format is the pcf  former um that follows the standard uh  four-point um you know x i would say um  formats um now there are outputs from  other pipelines secondary analysis  pipelines  that output several different formats um  one specifically i have in my mind is  the tsl500 platform they output several  different formats outside of the bcf  format and we're able to intake that as  well  um  now there are um  some uh platforms that um  do have very unconventional um output  files so we do have some methods that  allows us to upload the data via an xml  um  into the system or we do have in the  user interface also a way to upload um  this  in this case manually but with the xml  is an automated way  um  the other question was what are the  alteration types that are supported so  um  the um  the output size from a from a second  analysis typically gets into the copy  numbers diffusions and small variants  and so all of them are supported  we do support  anything that we can encode in  structural variant files  insertions the larger deletions uh  smaller deletions um  inversions and of course the copy  numbers as well  um  so the so there's all the structural  variants the small variants you know  smbs and delts  we do support other formats as well as  your quality of the um you can upload it  as well  into the into the into the pipeline we  we interpret that  um  so there is another question around if  we can incorporate too far so it depends  on like your  pipeline so  um we can't run the second analysis  pipeline and automatically upload into  our system as well so if you wish to use  a cost hue all the way to report report  that's possible as well  great thank you biata  okay  uh the next question that we have is how  long will it take for the professional  interpretation services  to provide me with the interpretive  comments  sure i can take that one as well so  we have two different  levels of service so the first one would  be the pre-curated version and that  would return expert comments within  just  a couple of minutes one to two minutes  usually  and that is drawing the information off  of our database you know based on over  over 200 000 curated cases and variants  so and pre-curated information as well  so whatever is currently present in the  knowledge base would be pulled in um to  the qci uh user interface um we also and  and in that case if there were a variant  that were novel that hadn't been covered  uh by the um the nf1 team  um then it would be returned as variant  not curated by n of one with the caveats  in appropriate places um but returning  gene and disease level content as  available  um we also have a curation service  option where  the team will curate every piece of  information for the report so every  novel variant um filling in information  on the the gene and disease level as  necessary doing any required updates and  that um  we we promise within up to three days um  but usually on average those are turned  around also within um on average about a  half day  okay thank you cheryl  next we have um  when you're showing the sample report  the slides were on a solid tumor sample  this qci interpret one process heme or  neuro-oncology samples  yes we do um the  both the the hydrogen knowledge base and  the um the nf1 team  expert interpretation knowledge base  both cover  um solid tumors heme  and  neural oncology as well and our oncology  experts span those  subspecialties as well so we have input  from clinical  hematologi